WEBVTT

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.940
Living in space, you may be called upon to
make split-second decisions at any time.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.820
In space, there's neither air around you,

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.030
nor ground to step upon.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.900
And a single, minor mistake may prove fatal.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.200
Once aboard a spaceship,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.870
you must continue making the right decisions.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.580
But that is what it means to live in space.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.250
Kato Marika was a master of these decisions.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.840
One with the true right to be a citizen of space.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.300
I'll be captain.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:38.010
I'll be a space pirate.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.660
Hi!

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.210
I see...

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.580
So, you're going to be a pirate.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:30.630
Yeah.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:35.210
I'll look at the sky, and you'll be up there, right?

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.590
I think I'll go when school allows.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.840
I want to graduate from high school.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.600
For now, let's have a lot of fun today!

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:44.220
Yeah!

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.220
We still have tons of summer break left.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:47.480
Let's go!

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.940
W-What?

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:57.900
We've come to pick you up.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:15.710
Kato... Marika.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:18.010
All right. Now your stamp.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.470
Okay, stamp.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.680
Stamp. Stamp. Stamp.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.060
We'll be going to all the government offices today, okay?

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.850
How many?

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.640
Department of Transportation, the Stellar Military.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.980
Department of Education, Department of Public Safety...

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.440
Including the other minor ones, there are almost twenty.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.660
We'll have a lot to carry.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.710
We're going down here?

00:03:58.710 --> 00:03:59.840
Run.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:01.840
Next.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.350
U-Um, now what?

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.350
There's this neat little clothing store...

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.980
F-For whom?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.270
This is the final one.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.740
Letter of Marque

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:39.340
Letter of Marque

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.630
So, now you're a pirate too...
Letter of Marque

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.130
How do you feel?

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:44.180
Well...

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:47.640
I guess I don't really feel like one,

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:48.930
at least not yet.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.600
You'd better get over that.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:56.310
A Letter of Marque is valid for fifty days.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.400
If you don't do any piracy during that time,

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.280
the letter is rescinded.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:05.490
That means the Bentenmaru has to go pirating,

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.570
since you got a new Letter.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:14.830
You have forty-nine days, nine hours, twenty-two minutes left.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:16.370
Seven weeks, huh?

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.880
I guess you'll have to find a way.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.380
Can you handle it?

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.550
You can do it, right?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.840
She doesn't have a choice.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.430
Um...

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.510
Have fun.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:40.440
Good luck, Marika.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.990
<i>Bentenmaru moving to normal flight.</i>

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:55.500
<i>No other transponders in the area.</i>

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.620
<i>Continuing toward destination...</i>

00:05:58.790 --> 00:05:59.380
What?

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:00.500
An attack?

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.420
Damage report!

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:02.880
Direct hit on the port side.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.130
Hull breach.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.510
No problems with the navigation systems.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:06.840
What about combat radar?

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.380
Stealth?

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:09.640
An ambush?

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.260
Oh, no. We have to get out of here!

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:13.930
Shields to maximum.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.430
Advance, while executing evasive maneuvers.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.730
Keep the sun behind us,

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:19.810
and use its gravity to re-accelerate.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.060
That should do it.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:22.860
There are more?

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:24.280
I'm surrounded?

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:25.820
Launch ECM!

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.280
Disperse chaff and beam-dispersal fields...

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:31.530
A direct hit to the engine room?

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.530
Output dropping...

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.450
Turn the ship around!

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:36.120
Target the weakest enemy,

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.580
and we can still get out of this!

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:45.500
We didn't get out of it...

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.130
<b>Captain, you are dead...</b>

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.340
And you've gone down.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.800
Everyone aboard has died.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:55.350
Is being a pirate really this difficult?

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:56.850
Well...

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:59.230
It doesn't happen often,

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:03.940
but you need to be ready for
times when it does get this bad.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:08.490
A captain must be able to laugh and make
decisions, regardless of how bad things are.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.360
Not like that.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.030
Okay, sixty minute break.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.660
Get some food and cool your head.
Then we'll discuss electronic warfare.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.540
Roger...

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:35.140
Well?

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.510
Are you getting used to it?

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:39.310
I don't know if I'm used to it yet...

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:42.480
It's better than when I started, though.

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:44.480
What's next?

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:45.940
Electronic warfare lecture.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.280
Then hand-to-hand combat training...

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.110
Try to stay alive until my class, okay?

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:53.570
I'll do my best...

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.450
Okay, now this one! This one!

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:06.170
Six hours of sleep,

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.920
then back up and at 'em...

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.300
One hundred and twenty hours into the voyage.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.680
She's trying pretty hard.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.550
We'd better hope she is...

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:20.560
At first, it felt like she was just going with the flow.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:23.270
But now, she's beginning to think for herself.

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.650
She's sharp.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:28.730
But it's gonna take another push or two.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:32.700
I think it's about time for the propellant.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.780
Our propellant has arrived.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:44.830
Chiaki Kurihara,

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:48.170
daughter of the Barbalusa's captain, Kenjo Kurihara.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:52.300
I'm honored to have been invited to this training.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:55.220
Chiaki?

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:56.970
What?

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.300
Don't speak so informally!

00:08:58.300 --> 00:08:59.640
Thanks for coming.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:00.390
I'm so happy...

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:04.230
I'm here for the special training!

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:05.980
I didn't come here to see you.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:07.980
That's just fine...

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.440
I'm so happy!

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:12.400
Chiaki!

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.650
Propellant's the right word.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.800
I'm going on ahead!

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:37.640
You learned about the history of pirates in school, right?

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:39.640
The colonies' war for independence

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:41.720
began at the Sea of the Morningstar.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:45.060
To bolster their military size,

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:47.020
for their fight against their overseers,

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.560
the Colony Federation issued

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.150
Letters of Marque to space pirates.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:54.150
So, why did the independence wars end?

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.190
Marika?

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.450
Because both the Colony Federation and

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:01.200
their suzerains were absorbed by the Galactic Empire.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.160
That's right.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.330
An enormous Galactic Empire fleet appeared,

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.580
and absorbed both sides

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:10.080
with its overwhelming power.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.880
That's scarily well made.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.460
Does she like crafts?

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:18.130
So everything ended before a final war could begin,

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:19.890
and they all lived happily ever after.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:23.180
Then what happened to the pirates?

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:27.020
That's right.

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:29.400
They're still pirating.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:29.900
Galactic Empire

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.770
The Galactic Empire respects each system's right to self-rule.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:36.900
Of course, they don't allow piracy,

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:37.650
but a vessel with a proper Letter of Marque isn't a pirate ship.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:41.740
Letter of Marque

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:44.620
We aren't pirates?

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.250
Not on the surface.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.580
If nothing else,

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:51.170
the Galactic Fleet doesn't engage in large operations

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:53.500
to pursue or eliminate pirates.

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:56.710
We're pirates, but we're not pirates...

00:10:57.260 --> 00:11:01.720
Interstellar law treats pirates as military forces.

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:05.430
Thus, we must be professional.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:09.480
Naturally, that includes pirate captains.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:30.120
Spaceships are really isolated out here.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.710
I was surprised at first.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:36.630
Once you set sail, there isn't anything else around.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.090
So you have to construct your own internal bearings.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.760
How big the ship is,

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:41.720
where it's going,

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.260
and where it is.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:48.060
Then, you decide for yourself where you are.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.520
It's kind of exciting.

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:53.600
So that's why you want to be a pirate?

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:58.480
I thought of you as a soft, little princess, but I can see I was wrong.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:11:59.690
I'm not?

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.030
Maybe you don't understand.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:05.200
When you pretend to be a ditz,
it creates problems for those around you.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.990
You need to cut the act.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:11.210
I cause problems?

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:14.500
If nothing else, you make me angry.

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:18.500
I don't really understand, but I'm sorry.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.880
That's exactly what I'm talking about...

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.050
Nothing.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:26.800
Look. We're almost there.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.570
Good work, you two.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:41.360
To return, do the opposite of what you just did.

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:42.610
Okay!

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:43.570
Roger.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:47.370
What's wrong?

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:52.450
Doing all this stuff won't make
you a pirate captain, will it?

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:54.960
It's too late for that.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.210
Ignorance is a sin.

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:58.540
Actually, it's worse. It's fatal.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:12:59.920
Everyone will die.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:03.760
But pirates don't need an honor student captain

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.090
whose sole skill is doing everything correctly.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:09.310
She doesn't look like a mere honor student to me.

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:11.810
She's in the gap between two places.

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.230
A deeper, darker gap

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:16.520
than you would guess by looking at it.

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:18.980
That is why

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:21.400
she chose space.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:35.870
For real?

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.370
That's right.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:41.460
We've taught you many things,
but there are some things we can't teach.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:45.050
You have to learn them for yourself.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:45.920
Ah...

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:48.220
Like what?

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:49.390
Courage.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:52.970
Our target is the Princess Apricot,

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:55.730
a luxury liner sailing the Galactic Corridor West-37.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.230
It's a simple pirating exercise.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.110
We disable their systems with electronic warfare,

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.360
then board the ship and start taking things.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:05.320
We'll also be featuring additional swordplay by the captain.

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:07.530
S-Swordplay?

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:09.200
We are pirates, you know.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.660
Pirates use swords.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:14.660
Kane's already gone ahead to set it up.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:18.790
Schnitzer will give you additional
sword and weapons training.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.790
As for the rest...

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.710
Allow me to do it too!

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:25.090
You're going to train with me?

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.260
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:28.510
I want to learn.

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:32.220
I've never done anything official.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:33.720
This is a good chance.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:37.680
Thanks, you two.

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:02.960
Space pirates?

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.290
You didn't know?

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:08.130
This galactic corridor has been known
as the "Pirate's Corridor" forever.

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:11.510
But pirates are just a legend, aren't they?

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:12.220
Right?

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:15.310
I heard that they were exterminated long ago,

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:18.850
and none are to be found, even on
the undeveloped border planets.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:22.310
Pirates in these modern times, huh?

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:25.900
A toast to our ship's safety, and to space pirates.

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:30.240
The luxury liner Princess Apricot

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:34.320
has just completed its twelfth FTL drive.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:39.040
We have arrived in Galactic Corridor West-37 as scheduled.

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:43.000
We will soon be at our closest
distance to the red giant Lambdall.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:45.960
Our course remains unchanged.

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:49.880
It will soon be midnight in the main hall.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:51.550
We hope all of our passengers

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:52.630
continue to enjoy the voyage...
It's almost time.

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:55.390
What?

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:58.640
You ladies are about to have an interesting experience.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.230
Could this be...

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:03.230
We're quite fortunate!

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:04.610
You already did it?

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:06.110
It's working?

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:07.900
We're broadcasting?

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:09.570
S-Sorry!

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:10.940
This is the Bentenmaru,

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:13.030
the pirate ship Bentenmaru!

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:18.830
I'm Captain Marika of the pirate ship Bentenmaru.

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:22.830
I'm the pirate ship captain, Captain Marika...

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:24.750
They're loving it.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:28.420
Not only are they being attacked by pirates, but the captain is a girl.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:30.050
They're lucky.

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:33.380
The Bentenmaru has completed its electronic attack

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:35.640
on the Princess Apricot's systems.

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:40.100
All Princess Apricot systems, including navigation,

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:43.060
are now under our control!

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:45.770
She's loving this...

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.020
Want to give it a try?

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:49.530
No, thanks.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:56.030
Basically, the Princess Apricot is now in our hands!

00:16:58.200 --> 00:16:59.950
Why are they all so happy?

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:01.660
W-What's going on?

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.540
Because pirates are coming.

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:04.750
Coming?

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.130
The Bentenmaru's main cannons

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:11.050
are locked on the Princess Apricot's bridge,

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:13.760
so escape or resistance would be utterly impossible!

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:18.470
I, Captain Marika, and my party are coming aboard!

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:22.930
All passengers, please prepare to hand over your valuables.

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:35.650
You did well for your first time.

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:39.910
All that's left now is for you to act like a captain.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.830
Hey, Schnitzer...

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.250
What?

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:47.460
You went pirating with Ririka...

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.670
I mean, Blaster Ririka, right?

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:53.460
Yeah, just like this.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:56.550
What was my mother like?

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.300
Why does it matter?

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.680
You're your own person.

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:01.810
And Ririka is Ririka.

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.850
Concentrate on the task at hand.

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.730
Yeah, you're right.

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:15.030
That's why I've come to space.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.490
A-Are they real pirates?

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:23.870
That's the space pirate ship Bentenmaru.

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:27.960
They bear a Letter of Marque and a long history.

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:33.420
In Galactic Empire space, pirates are an endangered species.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:35.880
You're fortunate.

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:37.090
Fortunate?

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.130
What will happen to us?

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:43.510
They might ask you to hand over your accessories...

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:44.890
But don't worry.

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:47.730
The liner company's insurance will cover the loss.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:04.530
I am Marika, Captain of the Bentenmaru.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:05.950
I've come to pirate.

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:08.250
Thank you all for your cooperation.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.670
That was a warning shot, of course.

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:13.670
Just to be safe,

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:17.590
we have temporarily disabled your surveillance system.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.840
If you fine people will comply with our demands,

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:23.470
you will return to port safely,

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:25.720
and you'll be among the lucky few

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:29.140
who have experienced a pirate raid and lived.

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:30.940
If you do decide to resist—

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:32.270
What will happen?

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:40.070
I wish to challenge the pirate captain to a duel.

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:42.490
I see these all the time...

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:44.160
Show-offs like you.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:48.540
If I win, I ask that you leave the Princess Apricot,

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:51.710
without laying a hand on the ladies.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:55.460
And if you lose?

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:58.960
If that happens, my body will simply return to the stars.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:11.440
She's looking pretty good.

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:13.440
She still isn't moving well.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:26.450
Prepare yourself!

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:32.540
I-I have died in vain...

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:35.880
Now, does anyone else have complaints?

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:38.250
If not, then do as I say.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:41.210
Hand over your valuables!

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:53.940
My dad's room, huh?

00:20:57.860 --> 00:21:01.740
I have a long way to go, don't I?

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:12.500
Sure you don't want to tell Kato goodbye, Kurihara?

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:13.790
I can wake her up if you want...

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:16.170
I'll prioritize rendezvousing with the Barbalusa.

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:19.130
Misa said there wouldn't be any problems with that.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:23.550
But next semester, you're returning to your old school, right?

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:26.050
You won't be able to see her for a while.

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:27.090
That's fine.

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:31.470
Seeing her ditzy face just makes me unhappy.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:33.060
By the way, Mr. Kane...

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:36.520
Aren't you going to change?

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:41.400
I like hearing everyone gasp when they see it.

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:42.780
That's creepy.

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:43.940
Excuse me.

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:44.860
Bye, Kurihara.

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:46.780
Gyah!

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:54.960
Flying alone, huh?

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.120
Trainee

00:21:58.120 --> 00:21:59.710
But you are not alone in space.
Trainee

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:02.460
But you are not alone in space.

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:08.220
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:11.390
Marika's First Day at Work
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:12.430
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:17.940
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:20.940
Welcome glory, let's breakthrough and fly out now, let's go!

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:24.320
Run towards an unlimited dimension. Come, let's accelerate beyond this

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:27.400
history that's to be known, regardless of time. Fly towards a destined future.

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:30.450
Just a fossil if you give up a miracle. Your decision is your best choice.

00:22:32.030 --> 00:22:39.370
There's another, unknown, me hiding in my heart.

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:44.250
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:48.090
How far?

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:50.760
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell! Go, go, ring, ring a bell!

00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:54.390
Until the end.

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:55.720
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell!

00:22:55.720 --> 00:22:59.060
You're lost and missing.

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:07.900
We're lost without a hope of any shelter.

00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:11.660
But why? What did we do? What did we do?

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:13.070
What should we do?

00:23:13.070 --> 00:23:16.240
From the world beyond shadows invade.

00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:20.540
We're destined to stop them with our lives.

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:26.590
So no matter where we go, as far as it takes

00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:30.840
we'll always believe in ourselves.

00:23:38.680 --> 00:23:40.850
Great resolve turns to everyday life,

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:42.600
and peace sets in.

00:23:43.130 --> 00:23:45.150
But that is only temporary.

00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:48.440
A pirate's days are never dull.

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:52.990
How will the girl pirate captain read the fierce winds?

00:23:54.360 --> 00:23:56.120
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:56.120 --> 00:23:57.650
The peace does not last.

00:23:57.650 --> 00:23:58.950
Look forward to it.

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:04.920
The Peace Does Not Last

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:15.440
But you are not alone in space...
